    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5417477/adjunct-nursing-clinical-undergraduate": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Nursing Clinical Undergraduate",
      "description": "Adjunct - Nursing Clinical Undergraduate Location 1 College Circle, Bangor, ME Job Type Part-Time Job Number 00978 Department Nursing Mngmt (1151) Division Adjunct Opening Date 07/21/2026 Closing Date 7/21/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description The Clinical Preceptor provides direct supervision and clinical instruction for groups of Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) students within the clinical practice setting. Working collaboratively with the School of Nursing (SON) course faculty, the Clinical Preceptor facilitates clinical learning experiences developed as part of the nursing curriculum. Through direct supervision, role modeling, and coaching, the Clinical Preceptor supports the development of students' clinical knowledge, technical skills, professional behaviors, clinical judgment, and critical thinking. The Clinical Preceptor promotes a safe, supportive, and engaging learning environment while providing formative and summative feedback regarding student performance using standardized evaluation tools. Example of Duties Qualified candidates with demonstrated clinical expertise are encouraged to apply. Participate in required clinical orientation sessions and educational activities offered by Husson University School of Nursing and the assigned clinical agency. Directly supervise a group of BSN nursing students in the assigned clinical setting in accordance with course learning outcomes, professional standards, and the policies of both the School of Nursing and the clinical agency. Facilitate student learning through clinical teaching, coaching, role modeling, and direct supervision while promoting safe, ethical, evidence-based nursing practice. Conduct pre- and post-clinical conferences using course objectives and learning activities. Provide timely, constructive feedback to students using standardized clinical evaluation tools. Communicate regularly with SON course faculty regarding student progress, concerns, and recommendations for additional support or remediation. Provide the SON course faculty with a summary of each clinical day, including student progress, learning opportunities, and any significant issues or concerns. Contribute objective performance feedback for midterm and final student evaluations using standardized evaluation criteria. Notify the SON course faculty promptly of student absences, injuries, illnesses, safety concerns, or professional conduct issues occurring during the clinical experience. Collaborate with SON course faculty to promote consistent clinical instruction and student success. Qualifications Current, active, and unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) license in the State of Maine. Bachelor's degree in Nursing (BSN) required; Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) preferred. Specialty certification relevant to the clinical area is desirable. Minimum of one (1) year of active clinical nursing experience required; three (3) or more years of active clinical practice preferred. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS General Physical Requirements Work is generally performed in a classroom, laboratory, clinical, online, office, or other instructional setting. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Physical Activities The essential functions of this position may require the ability to: Move about instructional, laboratory, clinical, office, or campus environments. Remain in a stationary position for extended periods while teaching, presenting, meeting with students, or performing related duties. Occasionally move, transport, or position instructional materials and equipment. Visual Requirements Must be able to read, prepare, evaluate, and review a variety of materials in both electronic and printed formats, and observe student activities as necessary to perform the essential functions of the position. Working Conditions Work is performed primarily in instructional, laboratory, clinical, office, or remote learning environments, depending on course assignment and modality. The position may require evening, weekend, or off-site instructional activities. APPLICATION INFORMATION Thank you for considering employment with Husson University. Please use our online application system to apply and track your application status. Husson University is an equal employment opportunity employer # AD We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5273788/adjunct-occupational-therapy": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Adjunct - Occupational Therapy Salary $0.00 Hourly Location 1 College Circle, Bangor, ME Job Type Part-Time Job Number 00881 Department Occup Therapy (1185) Division Adjunct Opening Date 03/17/2026 Closing Date 3/17/2027 12:00 AM Eastern Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description Husson University has been transforming students’ lives for over 100 years by preparing graduates for professional careers in current and emerging fields. The School of Occupational Therapy seeks qualified adjunct faculty to support our growing occupational therapy programs and contribute their clinical expertise to the education of future practitioners. Adjunct faculty play an important role in supporting student learning and professional development by delivering course content that reflects current occupational therapy practice. Courses are primarily taught on campus in a 15-week format, though hybrid or online delivery may be used when appropriate. Husson University is committed to building a diverse and inclusive academic community. We welcome applicants who can contribute to the educational experience of our students through their teaching, scholarship, and professional experience. Example of Duties Teach assigned occupational therapy course(s) using instructional strategies that support student engagement and professional reasoning Prepare course materials, assignments, and learning activities aligned with course objectives Assess student performance and provide timely, constructive feedback Maintain accurate records of grades and student progress in accordance with university policies Utilize the university’s learning management system to distribute course materials and manage course communication Communicate with program leadership regarding student progress or concerns Attend faculty meetings as requested Qualifications Required Qualifications Master's or Doctoral degree in Occupational Therapy from an accredited institution Current NBCOT certification Maine Occupational Therapy licensure or eligibility for licensure At least 3 years of clinical experience in occupational therapy practice Strong written and verbal communication skills Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching or clinical instruction experience Familiarity with occupational therapy educational standards and accreditation expectations Experience using learning management systems or instructional technologies Supplemental Information The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit and use hands to finger, handle, or feel. The employee frequently is required to reach with hands and arms. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, and talk or hear. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus. Thank you for considering employment with Husson University. To apply and inquire about your application status, please use our online application system. We kindly request that applicants do not email or call to check on their application status. Thank you for your understanding and adherence to our application process. Husson University is an equal employment opportunity employer #AD We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5505410/adjunct-instructor-in-english-remote": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in English (Remote)",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor in English (Remote) Salary $0.00 Biweekly Location REMOTE - WORK FROM HOME, ME Job Type Part-Time Remote Employment Remote Only Job Number 01060 Department Online Learning Instr (1350) Division Adjunct Opening Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date 1/5/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Max Number of Applicants 500 Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description Husson University in Bangor, ME, has been transforming students’ lives for over 100 years by inspiring and preparing them for professional careers in current and emerging fields through an education grounded in the sciences and humanities. Thousands of students have benefited from this transformative power of education, and we are committed to strategic decisions that ensure this impact continues well into the future. Husson University seeks to attract world-class adjunct faculty to enrich the educational experience of our professionally motivated students. We are committed to building a diverse faculty who excel in teaching and thrive in a multicultural environment. Candidates who can contribute to diversity and excellence through teaching, scholarship, and professional experience are especially encouraged to apply. The Division of Online and Distance Education at Husson University invites applications for a part-time adjunct faculty pool. This posting will remain open for a 90-day period to establish a pool of qualified candidates who may be considered for future online teaching or course development opportunities. Applications are reviewed as instructional and course development needs arise during the posting period. After the posting closes, applications may continue to be reviewed from the established pool based on departmental needs. Teaching and course development assignments are dependent upon factors such as student enrollment, program needs, course scheduling, and institutional priorities. Example of Duties Husson University is seeking dynamic individuals to teach online courses in English. Course instructors are content experts who focus on providing an elite educational experience for learners to improve their skill level and knowledge. Candidates with demonstrated expertise and professional experience in English are encouraged to apply. Qualifications An earned terminal degree in the discipline or a related field (doctoral degree preferred) Prior experience in online course instruction in higher education (preferred) Effective communication skills to convey subject matter clearly Strong organizational and time management skills Commitment to providing innovative and engaging online education Supplemental Information Thank you for considering employment with Husson University. To apply and inquire about your application status, please use our online application system. We kindly request that applicants do not email or call to check on their application status. Please note that inclusion in the adjunct pool does not guarantee employment or an offer of assignment. Candidates will be contacted by the Division of Online and Distance Education only if selected for consideration for a specific opening. This posting will close after the designated period. Candidates who wish to be considered for future opportunities are encouraged to apply to new postings as they become available. Thank you for your understanding and adherence to our application process. Undergraduate Courses: - Master’s Prepared: Up to $933.33 per credit hour* - Doctoral or Equivalent Prepared: Up to $1,016.67 per credit hour* Graduate Courses: - Master’s Prepared: Up to $1,016.67 per credit hour* - Doctoral or Equivalent Prepared: Up to $1,100.00 per credit hour* *Rate is dependent upon the number of students enrolled in the course assigned. Lab Sections (Undergraduate): - Master’s Prepared: $1,150.00 per credit hour - Doctoral or Equivalent Prepared: $1,250.00 per credit hour Online Course Development: Proposal or development fees range from $500.00 to $3,000.00, depending upon the complexity of the assignment. Husson University is an equal employment opportunity employer #AD We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
