    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5114587/instructor-or-assistant-professor-accounting": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor – Accounting",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor – Accounting Location 1 College Circle, Bangor, ME Job Type Full-Time Job Number 00810 Department Accounting (1111) Division Faculty Opening Date 10/16/2025 Closing Date Continuous Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description The School of Accounting in the College of Business invites applications for an Instructor or Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2026. The primary responsibility of all full-time faculty of the University is the scholarly teaching of students in the courses and sections that are assigned. The successful candidate must demonstrate an ongoing commitment to quality teaching, scholarship, and professional service, as well as excellent communication and interpersonal skills. The candidate will be expected to deliver experiential and applied learning to students. All course delivery and assessment data will be aligned and collected in accordance with the International Accreditation Council for Business Education (IACBE) accreditation standards. Courses will be taught in face-to-face classrooms, hybrid environments, and via online delivery. Additionally, this professor will advise students regarding a variety of career goals and courses. Example of Duties Teaching: Teach 24 credits per academic year; Courses taught may be in the areas of introduction to accounting, intermediate and advanced accounting, managerial accounting, cost accounting, federal tax, non-profit accounting and internships as well as possibly other courses in the faculty member’s area of expertise; Instruct and assist in the growth and success of a diverse population of students through careful preparation of course materials, effective teaching methodologies, and informed critical feedback on assignments and discussions; Prepare course materials and use appropriate teaching techniques which may include but are not limited to delivering lectures, leading discussions, and conducting experiential learning opportunities in face-to-face classes, hybrid environments, and online through Canvas; Deliver experiential and applied learning to students while incorporating the technology available on campus; Contribute to the development and revision of course content and instructional materials, textbook and equipment selection, and assessment strategies; Align all course delivery and collect assessment data in accordance with the International Accreditation Council for Business Education accreditation standards. Apply emerging technologies and advances as necessary to perform duties in an efficient, organized and timely manner. Maintain current knowledge of instructional methods and new technologies pertinent to areas of assignment; Scholarship and Professional Activity: Remain current in areas of expertise through continual study and scholarship in discipline and through involvement in professional organizations; Provide assistance with curriculum development; Service: Connect with local firms for internships and job placements, Advising Accounting Society, Participate in School, College, and University meetings, retreats, committees, and activities (open house, and/or student recruitment projects); Follow the policies and procedures outlined in the Faculty Handbook; Advising: Advise students in the College of Business according to the Husson University Advising Manual; Work with students and employers in professional settings, internships, field placements, and similar work-related situations as needed; Employ University retention strategies; Maintain weekly office hours to meet with students regarding class work, course registration, program declaration and career preparation. Qualifications Master’s degree (MBA or Masters in Accounting) or equivalent plus CPA or CMA and several years of industry experience required; Terminal degree (PhD, DBA) is desired; CPA or CMA is preferred. Experience: Demonstrated excellence in teaching with specific knowledge and ability to teach undergraduate courses in a variety of business topic areas. Knowledge and ability to teach face-to-face, in a hybrid environment or online. Industry experience required Ability to lead and strong communication skills Connections with local and Maine accounting firms preferred Mastery of appropriate computer operation skills. The successful candidate will be dynamic, energetic, creative, and engaging and have strong interpersonal and communication skills, demonstrating a commitment to cultural diversity and inclusive education. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to Husson University’s mission and to the highest ethical standards. Supplemental Information The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform their functions. Effectively communicate with students and other faculty Read and interpret with vision ability for close and distance vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus Ability to lift and move materials weighing up to twenty-five pounds Sit or stand for extended periods of time Bend, kneel, and reach with the use of hands and arms Utilize telephone, email, and other university communications systems Operate a computer, copier, printer, television, and projector #NT We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5288405/instructor-science-lab-coordinator": {
      "title": "Instructor/Science Lab Coordinator",
      "description": "Instructor/Science Lab Coordinator Location 1 College Circle, Bangor, ME Job Type Full-Time Job Number 00889 Department Math & Sci (1166) Division Faculty Opening Date 03/27/2026 Closing Date Continuous Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description Husson University has an opening for an Instructor/ Science Lab Coordinator with experience working in a lab setting and teaching at the university level. The Laboratory Coordinator component of this position includes responsibility for the daily operations of the labs, including Chemistry, Biology, and Anatomy & Physiology. Daily operations include maintaining and operating equipment, maintaining lab inventories, ordering equipment and supplies for the labs, and maintaining physical and written safety requirements of the labs. The Lab Coordinator is also responsible for preparing necessary lab materials for daily lab instruction. The Lab Coordinator facilitates lab instruction by adjuncts and has supervisory responsibility over student lab assistants working in the science labs. The faculty component of this position may include responsibilities for teaching and spearheading Husson’s on-campus programs, including Animal Care and Behavior. The department determines specific teaching assignments, but the teaching load is a minimum of three credit hours per semester. Example of Duties The successful candidate will possess the necessary organizational and interpersonal skills to carry out the following duties. General Lab Maintenance and Safety Compliance: Maintaining general lab equipment including cleaning and inventory Effective and proactive ordering of equipment and supplies for all the science labs and off-site partner animal care facilities Maintaining, installing, troubleshooting, and operating laboratory equipment Maintaining safe working conditions for all instructors and students in the labs using appropriate inventory, equipment, and storage Safely managing the collection and disposal of lab waste Maintaining safety paperwork in accordance with federal, state, and Husson University policies Maintaining standard operating procedures for lab safety and waste management Training personnel in site-specific laboratory safety Upholding lab cleanliness and appearance Supervision and Leadership: Preparing weekly lab materials Training students and other lab instructors to operate laboratory equipment Coordinating weekly meetings for General Biology and Microbiology labs Coordinating assessment data reporting and compliance for biology labs In coordination with the Chair, developing the lab schedule for the academic year In cooperation with other relevant Science faculty, hiring and supervising student workers Instructor Duties: Teach, monitor, and consult on on-campus programs, including Animal Care and Behavior Teach and assess student performance in lab courses Advise and mentor undergraduate students as needed in science majors Other responsibilities as assigned Qualifications Required Must have a minimum M.S. in the sciences with both teaching and laboratory management experience. Must be able to work independently and function collegially and effectively within a team environment. Must be comfortable preparing solutions, media and cultures, and operating and maintaining lab instruments. Technical/administrative experience in laboratory operations and safety compliance is a plus. Preferred PhD in the sciences and 3+ years’ experience in laboratory management Experience in supervising and mentoring student laboratory assistants OSHA and HAZWOPER training Supplemental Information Physical Requirements Work Environment: The job may require the employee to stand for extended periods of time. The position has a significant laboratory component, with specified protocols for methods and safety. This position may require independent development of instrumentation methods and interaction with technical support teams from instrument suppliers. HUSSON UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER **Exact compensation may vary based on skills, experience, and location.** #NT We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5461268/international-enrollment-manager": {
      "title": "International Enrollment Manager",
      "description": "International Enrollment Manager Salary $65,039.20 - $76,560.42 Biweekly Location 1 College Circle, Bangor, ME Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01025 Department International Initiatives (2122) Division Staff Opening Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date Continuous Academic Year No Description Benefits Description Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment Management, the International Enrollment Manager leads the University’s international recruitment, supports global engagement efforts and provides campus-based support for enrolled international students. This role is responsible for international student recruitment, application review, and oversight of institutional compliance within the Student and Exchange Visitor Program system. The International Enrollment Manager develops and maintains partnerships with international and domestic organizations, supports international students throughout their enrollment lifecycle and promotes study abroad participation among Husson students. The position collaborates with internal campus departments and with external stakeholders to advance the University’s global initiatives, enrollment goals and positive student experience. Example of Duties Recruitment and Admissions: • Recruit international students through multi-channel strategies including social media, digital communications, phone or virtual meeting outreach and annual domestic and international travel including evenings and weekends as needed. • Utilize institutional CRM and SIS systems to document and record interactions, student data, enrollment status and financial documentation. • Evaluate international applications in collaboration with the Director of Admissions and admissions processing staff. • Represent the University at international recruitment fairs, virtual events, campus events, and partner programs. • Expand recruitment pipelines through partnerships with U.S. secondary schools enrolling international students. • Coordinate with the Graduate Admissions Division regarding international applicants for campus-based graduate programs and provide necessary SEVIS documentation for admitted graduate students. Partnership Development: • Develop and maintain relationships with international high schools, colleges, universities, governments, and international partner organizations. • Build relationships with community colleges to support international transfer student recruitment. • Establish and sustain professional networks with local, national, and international organizations. • Consult regularly with Admissions, Financial Aid, Student Services, and academic departments. • Execute international recruitment initiatives while remaining within the Office of International Initiatives annual budget. • Generate academic and demographic reports for recruited international students and those students studying abroad through university partnerships. • Supervise work study students supporting the Office of International Initiatives, as needed. • Consult with academic and administrative departments to ensure continuation of services for accepted students and provide prospect and applicant data to academic departments. • Remain current on changes in university policy and curriculum. Compliance: • Maintain and monitor immigration services and compliance with Immigration & Customs Enforcement (ICE) regulations for the Student Exchange & Visitor Program (SEVP) as the institution’s Principal Designated School Official (PDSO). • Manage and develop international recruitment procedures, create weekly enrollment reports, and assist in the completion of annual surveys. • Collaborate with academic departments and advisors to provide application guidelines and processes for students interested in pursuing study abroad opportunities through institutional partnerships. Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree in higher education or related field preferred. • Three to five years of progressive experience in international admissions or enrollment services. • Demonstrated knowledge of Student and Exchange Visitor Program regulations and compliance requirements involving F-1 Student Visas. • Experience with international recruitment strategies and partnership development. • Strong cross-cultural communication and interpersonal skills. Supplemental Information HUSSON UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER **Exact compensation may vary based on skills, experience, and location.** #NT We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5473539/online-course-developers-instructors-bs-wildlife-care-rehab-and-certificate": {
      "title": "Online Course Developers & Instructors BS Wildlife Care & Rehab. and Certificate Aquatic Animal Care",
      "description": "Online Course Developers & Instructors BS Wildlife Care & Rehab. and Certificate Aquatic Animal Care Location REMOTE - WORK FROM HOME, ME Job Type Part-Time Job Number 01043 Department Online Learning Instr (1350) Division Adjunct Opening Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 12/4/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Max Number of Applicants 500 Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description Husson University in Bangor, ME, has been transforming students’ lives for over 100 years by inspiring and preparing them for professional careers in current and emerging fields through an education grounded in the sciences and humanities. Thousands of students have benefited from this transformative power of education, and we are committed to strategic decisions that ensure this impact continues well into the future. Husson University seeks to attract world-class adjunct faculty to enrich the educational experience of our professionally motivated students. We are committed to building a diverse faculty, part-time and full-time, who excel in teaching and thrive in a multicultural environment. Candidates who can contribute to diversity and excellence through teaching, scholarship, and professional experience are especially encouraged to apply. Example of Duties Husson University is seeking dynamic individuals to develop online courses for a bachelor’s degree in Wildlife Care and Rehabilitation and an undergraduate certificate in Aquatic Animal Care. Online course developers and instructors are content experts who focus on providing an elite educational experience for learners to improve their skill level and knowledge. Course developers work closely with instructional designers and leadership to define expectations throughout the course build process. Candidates with demonstrated expertise and professional experience in the following course topics are encouraged to apply: Aquatic Animal Care Aquatic Animal Habitats Introduction to Wildlife Care and Management Human Dimensions of Wildlife Care and Rehabilitation Designing Captive Wildlife Experiences Wildlife Rescue, Transport, and Triage Research Design for Animal Studies North American Wildlife Qualifications An earned terminal degree in the discipline or a related field (doctoral degree preferred) Prior experience in online course design and instruction in higher education (preferred) Previous experience working in wildlife care and rehabilitation or aquatic animal care (preferred) Effective communication skills to convey subject matter clearly Strong organizational and time management skills Commitment to providing innovative and engaging online education Supplemental Information Undergraduate Courses: - Master’s Prepared: Up to $933.33 per credit hour* - Doctoral or Equivalent Prepared: Up to $1,016.67 per credit hour* Graduate Courses: - Master’s Prepared: Up to $1,016.67 per credit hour* - Doctoral or Equivalent Prepared: Up to $1,100.00 per credit hour* *Rate is dependent upon the number of students enrolled in the course assigned. Lab Sections (Undergraduate): - Master’s Prepared: $1,150.00 per credit hour - Doctoral or Equivalent Prepared: $1,250.00 per credit hour Online Course Development: Proposal or development fees range from $1,500.00 to $5,000.00, depending upon the complexity of the assignment. Thank you for considering employment with Husson University. Please use our online application system to apply and track your application status. Kindly refrain from contacting us via email or phone regarding application updates. Thank you for your understanding and adherence to our application process. Husson University is an equal employment opportunity employer #AD We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
