    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5461244/regional-undergraduate-admissions-recruiter-nh-vt": {
      "title": "Regional Undergraduate Admissions Recruiter- NH/VT",
      "description": "Regional Undergraduate Admissions Recruiter- NH/VT Salary $45,884.90 - $47,049.00 Biweekly Location REMOTE - WORK FROM HOME, ME Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01024 Department Admissions (3111) Division Staff Opening Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date Continuous Academic Year No Description Benefits Description Full-Time Results Oriented Admissions Recruiter (Remote – Must reside in New Hampshire or Vermont). We are currently seeking a driven and results-oriented individual to join our team as a full-time Admissions Recruiter. This position will be remote, with a focus on recruiting prospective students from the regions of New Hampshire and Vermont. As an Admissions Recruiter, you will play a crucial role in the entire admissions recruitment cycle, engaging with high schools, college fairs, school counselors, teachers and prospective students and families both in person and virtually. Example of Duties Execute a comprehensive admissions recruitment strategy tailored to New Hampshire and Vermont regions, as well as additional territories not requiring travel, aiming to attract a diverse pool of prospective students. Develop and maintain strong relationships with school counselors and secondary school faculty members in the name of Husson University for the purpose of recruiting new students to the University. Represents the university at various high school college fairs and other events to promote our programs and offerings. Develops and maintains an overall knowledge of each program of study so that questions may be discussed with prospective students. Maintain accurate visit and recruiting records for all high schools in assigned territory. Assisting prospective students in the college enrollment process by phone, email, social networking and traditional mail is required. Travel and work flexible hours to recruit high school students through presentations at high school, fairs, and collaborative work with partners, schools or community groups and other off-campus events as needed. Extensive regional travel required in the fall and spring seasons, during the week and weekends, for the purposes of new student recruitment throughout New Hampshire and Vermont. Travel outside the primary assigned territories may occasionally be required to support recruitment outreach efforts. Work regionally with alumni for engagement and recruitment purposes. Occasional travel to campus will be required for training and special events. Collaborate with the admissions team to evaluate applications and make informed decisions regarding admissions. Adapt to changing recruitment trends and implement innovative strategies to achieve recruitment targets. Other miscellaneous duties may be assigned. Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Experience: 2+ years in related field preferred, especially if in college admissions or sales. Supplemental Information HUSSON UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER **Exact compensation may vary based on skills, experience, and location.** #NT We offer a comprehensive benefits package. Visit our website at Husson University for a complete list of benefits. Employer Husson University Address 1 College Circle Bangor, Maine, 04401 Phone (207) 941-7070 Website http://www.husson.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/husson/jobs/5308832/remote-adjunct-course-instructors-for-bs-animal-care-and-behavior-ms-animal-be": {
      "title": "Remote Adjunct - Course Instructors for BS Animal Care and Behavior, MS Animal Behavior and Welfare",
      "description": "Remote Adjunct - Course Instructors for BS Animal Care and Behavior, MS Animal Behavior and Welfare Location REMOTE - WORK FROM HOME, ME Job Type Part-Time Remote Employment Remote Only Job Number 00906 Department Online Learning Instr (1350) Division Adjunct Opening Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date 1/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Max Number of Applicants 500 Academic Year Yes Description Benefits Description Husson University in Bangor, ME, has been transforming students’ lives for over 100 years by inspiring and preparing them for professional careers in current and emerging fields through an education grounded in the sciences and humanities. Thousands of students have benefited from this transformative power of education, and we are committed to strategic decisions that ensure this impact continues well into the future. Husson University seeks to attract world-class adjunct faculty to enrich the educational experience of our professionally motivated students. We are committed to building a diverse faculty who excel in teaching and thrive in a multicultural environment. Candidates who can contribute to diversity and excellence through teaching, scholarship, and professional experience are especially encouraged to apply. The Division of Online and Distance Education at Husson University invites applications for a part-time adjunct faculty pool. This posting will remain open for a 90-day period to establish a pool of qualified candidates who may be considered for future online teaching or course development opportunities. Applications are reviewed as instructional and course development needs arise during the posting period. After the posting closes, applications may continue to be reviewed from the established pool based on departmental needs. Teaching and course development assignments are dependent upon factors such as student enrollment, program needs, course scheduling, and institutional priorities. Example of Duties Husson University is seeking dyn